<title>USA: Computer Sciences takes control of Danish co.</title>
<headline>Computer Sciences takes control of Danish co.</headline>
<dateline>EL SEGUNDO, Calif. 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Computer Sciences Corp said Monday it has completed the acquisition of a 50 percent shareholding of Danish company Dan Computer Management.</p>
<p>The acquisition gives Computer Sciences a majority stake in Dan, having already acquired 75 percent of Datacentralen A/S, which owned the other 50 percent of Dan, earlier this year.</p>
<p>Dan provides central operating services to the Danish government and commercial markets.</p>
<p>Computer Sciences has 40,000 employees and offers services including management consulting and business re-engineering.</p>
